At least eight (8) years’ post admission relevant work experience three (3) of which should be at a senior lecturer or supervisory role;
Bachelor’s Degree in Law (LL.B) from a recognized university;
Master’s Degree in Law (LL.M) from a recognized university;
Post-graduate Diploma in Law;
An advocate of the High Court of Kenya with current practicing certificate;
Member of the Law Society of Kenya in good standing;
Certificate in management course lasting four (4) weeks will be an added advantage;
Fulfilled the requirements of Chapter six of the Constitution; and
Proficiency in Computer Applications.

