Job Description:
Duties and Responsibilities
Duties and responsibilities at this will include:-
Spearheading the development, implementation and review of meteorological training and research policies, regulations and guidelines;
Coordinating the development and maintenance of effective educational programs in the Institute and promote the improvement of teaching and learning;
Spearheading the development of training and research programs;
Overseeing capacity building and skill development in the field of Meteorology and related applied sciences;
Facilitating the advancement of the science of meteorology and technology through research and development;
Coordinating research on weather and climate modelling;
Fostering partnerships with other training and research institutions;
Spearheading preparation, assessment and evaluation of the Meteorological Training and Research curricula in accordance with the WMO’s Programmes on Education and Training and Government guidelines;
approving the institutes’ budgets and work plans;
training, developing and deploying of meteorological services staff; and
Managing the institutes’ performance.
For appointment to this grade, a candidate must have:-
Served as Deputy Director, Meteorological Services, CSG 6 in the public service for a minimum period of three (3) years;
(A Bachelors Degree in Meteorology from a university recognized in Kenya;
OR
A Bachelors Degree in Mathematics and Physics plus a Post-Graduate Diploma in Meteorology or equivalent qualification from a recognized University in Kenya;
A Masters degree in Meteorology, Climate Change, Disaster Management, Environment, Hydrology, Water Resources, Geo-information Science, Oceanography, Marine or equivalent qualification from a university recognized in Kenya;
A Certificate in Operational Training Course in Meteorology offered at the Institute for Meteorological Training and Research in Kenya;
A Membership to a relevant professional body;
Demonstrated professional competence, managerial and leadership capabilities as reflected in work performance and results; and
Demonstrated a clear understanding of National Development Polices, Goals, Legislations and ability to integrate them in the climate change functions.
