Job Description:
Duties and Responsibilities
Duties and responsibilities at this will include:-
Coordinating meteorological services in the counties
Verifying and validating the accuracy and timeliness of the Meteorological data, charts analysis and forecast products;
Providing Meteorological information database to users;
Interpreting remotely sensed data;
Preparing tailor made weather forecast for various applications
Preparing meteorological advisories, alerts warnings for various sectors;
Down scaling and disseminating meteorological information
Developing and reviewing meteorological curricula
Preparing serve weather products for application in various sector;
Marketing and branding of meteorological products
Analyzing air quality data
Developing climate change scenarios; collecting and collating data for publication
Generating and updating weekly, monthly and seasonal weather and climate bulletins;
Coordinating meteorological operation at the airports
Carrying out research in meteorology and related sciences.
Providing training and capacity building on meteorology and related sciences
Conducting public education and outreach programmes
For appointment to this grade, a candidate must have:-
Served as Principal Meteorologist CSG ‘8’ or its equivalent from the Public Service for a minimum period of three (3) years;
A Bachelors Degree in Meteorology or its equivalent qualification from a recognized university in Kenya;
OR
Aa Bachelors Degree in Mathematics and Physics plus a post graduate Diploma in Meteorology or its equivalent from a university recognized in Kenya;
A Certificate in operational Training Course lasting not less than six months from a recognized institution;
Demonstrated professional competence as reflected in the work performance and results; and
Clear understanding of National goals, values and principles of governance.
